course: dictionary
lesson: 7255
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «The pigeon sat on the windowsill, pecking at crumbs.» Pecking at crumbs is what a bird does, so pigeon means the bird here.
explain: «He was a homing pigeon, trained to fly home over hundreds of miles.» The words homing and trained tell you this is a special kind of pigeon, not just any bird in the park. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence?
explain: Some words belong to set phrases. «Put the letter in your pigeonhole» means a small box for letters, not a bird at all. «Pigeon-toed» means having feet that turn inwards. Phrases like these are learned by their meaning, not by taking each word on its own.
fact: A pigeon is a grey, or brown and white, bird with a small head and a round body.
fact: Pigeons are very common in towns and cities.
fact: A homing pigeon is trained to fly home over long distances, and was once used to carry messages.
fact: «Carrier pigeon» means a pigeon used to carry messages.
fact: «Pigeonhole» means a small box for letters, and «pigeon-toed» means having feet that turn inwards.
exercise: «The pigeon sat on the windowsill, pecking at crumbs.» What is a pigeon? | A kind of cake | A type of shoe | *A grey or brown and white bird | A small box for letters
exercise: Real pigeons eat seeds and grain, not eggs. What do real pigeons eat? | Fish from the river | *Seeds and grain | Snakes | Eggs from other birds' nests
exercise: «Put the letter in your pigeonhole.» What is a pigeonhole? | A pigeon that is lost | *A small box for letters | A soft cushion for sitting on | A bird's nest in a tree
test: «A homing pigeon taken far away will fly straight back to its own loft.» What does a homing pigeon do? | *Flies straight back home | Waits for someone to feed it | Sleeps in the loft all day | Hides from the rain
test: Pigeons carried messages in wars. What was one job pigeons did in wars? | Building bridges | Guarding castles | *Carrying messages | Pulling carts
exam: «Carrier pigeon» is a phrase. What does it mean, and which clue word helped you? | A bird that cannot fly, because of the word carrier | *A pigeon used to carry messages, because of the word carrier | A pigeon that eats carrots, because of the word pigeon | A lost bird in a city, because of the word pigeon
